{"slug":"second-largest","title":"Second Largest","topic":"basics","difficulty":"medium","order":57,"tags":["arrays","min-max","one-pass"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Tracking two records in one pass","body":["To find the largest you keep one record. To find the second largest you keep two, `first` and `second`, and update both while you walk through the array once. Sorting the array would also work, but one pass is simpler and does less work.","For each element `x` there are three cases:",{"list":["`x` is bigger than `first`: the old first becomes the second, and `x` is the new first.","`x` is not bigger than `first`, but it is bigger than `second` and **different from** `first`: it is the new second.","otherwise nothing changes."]},"The \"different from `first`\" part matters when the largest value appears more than once: here the second largest means the second largest **distinct** value. Start both records at a number smaller than any element, because you do not yet know the first value."]},"statement":["You are given `n` integers, at least two of them different. Print the second largest **distinct** value.","For `5 9 9 3` the largest is 9 and the second largest is 5."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `n`. The second line has `n` integers."],"outputFormat":["The second largest distinct value."],"constraints":["2 <= n <= 1000","-10^9 <= each number <= 10^9","At least two different values exist."],"examples":[{"input":"4\n5 9 9 3\n","output":"5\n","note":"The largest is 9, the second largest distinct value is 5."},{"input":"3\n-4 -8 -4\n","output":"-8\n","note":"The largest is -4, the second is -8."}],"hints":["Keep two variables, `first` and `second`, both starting very low (for example -2 * 10^18).","If `x > first`, shift: `second = first`, then `first = x`.","Otherwise, if `x > second` and `x != first`, set `second = x`."],"starter":{"python":"n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.nextLong();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["One pass keeps the two best distinct values seen so far. A new maximum pushes the old maximum down to second place; a value that is between the two (and not equal to the maximum) replaces the second."],"complexity":"Time O(n), space O(1) besides the input.","code":{"python":"n = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\nfirst = -2 * 10 ** 18\nsecond = -2 * 10 ** 18\nfor x in a:\n    if x > first:\n        second = first\n        first = x\n    elif x > second and x != first:\n        second = x\nprint(second)\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    long long first = -2000000000000000000LL;\n    long long second = -2000000000000000000LL;\n    for (long long x : a) {\n        if (x > first) {\n            second = first;\n            first = x;\n        } else if (x > second && x != first) {\n            second = x;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << second << endl;\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = sc.nextLong();\n\n        long first = Long.MIN_VALUE;\n        long second = Long.MIN_VALUE;\n        for (long x : a) {\n            if (x > first) {\n                second = first;\n                first = x;\n            } else if (x > second && x != first) {\n                second = x;\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(second);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"4\n5 9 9 3\n","output":"5\n"},{"input":"3\n-4 -8 -4\n","output":"-8\n"},{"input":"2\n1 2\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"2\n2 1\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"4\n7 7 7 8\n","output":"7\n"},{"input":"4\n8 7 7 7\n","output":"7\n"},{"input":"5\n1 2 3 4 5\n","output":"4\n"},{"input":"5\n5 4 3 2 1\n","output":"4\n"},{"input":"2\n-1000000000 1000000000\n","output":"-1000000000\n"},{"input":"1000\n474311817 -594283940 -722043497 260203771 -66565604 210784575 -521449871 30601453 -5364498 -105975186 94113082 266045652 -266709742 -651717931 636216716 519870322 -314495666 -710647340 364601822 765182568 977202053 456068915 -19854536 -888080589 -137704962 390938737 -572423849 258628085 -606583967 -640993507 173234465 603275651 -943193394 -601459338 205237658 -108649657 -586727642 292587683 -135702309 -167967163 -541271761 258798464 902114224 -572649789 -839677964 774699237 -180724860 950266562 772964313 840653823 -482601374 899630328 -934840726 334379350 212987919 -616663573 -395188467 -884706559 189555792 783855674 -104085372 -214755708 833021013 -768482015 -505756579 852596987 -247341671 448461912 -149184913 -538508650 244495852 -929282118 -864127975 -237672710 -287556143 123341177 722236646 -595049722 392403159 -281966914 -481030822 206830771 -708502505 -849884334 938888583 455373267 345834955 402813803 322995979 887058283 120942971 -281054984 -343842783 -849254036 -354640425 556162507 -599363272 67521316 758978958 -430695357 -751894466 420553588 -959731661 -786670461 -100516631 -274019044 795333560 -779556139 882926982 602755835 371964881 -676448046 267070877 138573835 352677342 -545318527 302475284 -908077193 -7266135 313132900 -568941663 354055014 -9580334